 "meter": [
  "THE ROUTE \u00b7 WHAT IS COMING, AND WHY"
 ],
 "open": [
  false
 ],
 "note": [
  "THE ROADMAP, and the only one in the deck - say it once, clearly, and then do not repeat it.\n\nThree things a later paper needs before it can use your conclusion: what you actually said, what you relied on, and which parts anybody checked. A PDF gives you the first, sometimes. It does not give you the other two in any form a machine - or a hurried human - can follow.\n\nThen the route across the bottom. One paper, frozen. Its claims and the dependencies between them. One theorem's chain pulled out of that graph. And then, honestly, where the whole thing stops - because it does stop, and the last act of this talk is about exactly where.\n\nThe promise on the last line matters more than it looks: every number from here on is read out of this repository's own logs. Where nobody has measured something, the frame says nobody measured it."
 ],
 "cumulative": false
